{
  "id": "chaplygin-free-sleigh-fourth-science",
  "name": "Free Chaplygin sleigh: nonholonomic alignment",
  "category": "physics",
  "description": "Planar rigid body with an ideal knife-edge constraint. Forward speed and angular speed exchange energy. For the default positive offset and nonzero initial angular speed, turning decays toward forward straight motion without friction; zero offset keeps angular speed constant, and negative offset reverses the selected straight-motion direction. Coordinates follow the mass center, not the knife edge. Positive mass/inertia, offset a; omit forces, slip, friction, impacts and control. Default m=J=a=1, forward speed0, angular speed1, angle/position0. Energy0.5*m*u^2+0.5*(J+m*a^2)*omega^2 is conserved; asymptotic forward speed sqrt(2). Twenty seconds, RK4 step0.02. Original mathematical transcription/derivation; parameters are illustrative, not empirical calibration. Signed net-rate flows represent derivatives, not nonnegative physical transfers. No clamps or hidden resets.",
  "source": "https://arxiv.org/abs/1909.01130",
  "reference": "S. P. Kuznetsov (2019), Complex dynamics in generalizations of the Chaplygin sleigh, arXiv:1909.01130, equations2.1-2.2 with external force zero. No paper trajectory/chaos claim reproduced.",
